## Technology Stack
- **Language**: Java 21
- **Framework**: Spring Boot 3.x
- **Build**: Maven (use `mvn` commands, not `./mvnw` unless wrapper is present)
- **Test framework**: JUnit 5 + Mockito + Spring Boot Test
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Spring Data JPA
- **Other key dependencies**: Lombok, Jackson

## Package Structure
```
src/main/java/com/{your-group}/{your-artifact}/
├── controller/     — @RestController classes only, no business logic
├── service/        — Interfaces + implementations, business logic lives here
├── repository/     — Spring Data JPA repositories
├── model/          — JPA entities
├── dto/            — Request/response DTOs (use Java records)
├── config/         — @Configuration classes
└── exception/      — Custom exception classes + @ControllerAdvice
```

The test structure mirrors src/main:
```
src/test/java/com/{your-group}/{your-artifact}/
├── controller/     — MockMvc-based controller tests
├── service/        — Unit tests with Mockito
└── integration/    — @SpringBootTest integration tests (use sparingly)
```

## Naming Conventions
- Controllers: `{Entity}Controller.java` — e.g. `ItemController.java`
- Services: `{Entity}Service.java` (interface) + `{Entity}ServiceImpl.java` (impl)
- Repositories: `{Entity}Repository.java`
- Entities: singular noun — `Item`, not `Items`
- DTOs: `{Entity}CreateRequest`, `{Entity}UpdateRequest`, `{Entity}Response`
- Test classes: `{ClassName}Test.java` — mirrors the class under test exactly
- Test methods: `{methodName}_when{Condition}_should{ExpectedBehaviour}()`

## Coding Standards

### Required on all new code
- `@Slf4j` on every class that logs (use `log.info/warn/error`, never `System.out`)
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` for constructor injection (never `@Autowired` on fields)
- `@Transactional` on service methods that write to the database
- `@Valid` on all `@RequestBody` parameters in controllers
- `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank` etc. on DTO fields that are required

### Error handling pattern
```java
// Throw domain exceptions from service layer
throw new ResourceNotFoundException("Item not found: " + id);

// Handle in a single @ControllerAdvice (already exists at exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java)
// Do NOT add try-catch in controllers — let the advice handle it
```

### Response patterns
```java
// Use ResponseEntity with explicit status codes
return ResponseEntity.ok(itemService.findAll());
return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(itemService.create(request));
return ResponseEntity.noContent().build();  // for DELETE

// Never return null from a controller method
// Never return Optional from a controller method — resolve it in the service
```

### DTO pattern (Java records)
```java
// Request DTO
public record ItemCreateRequest(
    @NotBlank String name,
    @NotNull @Positive BigDecimal price
) {}

// Response DTO
public record ItemResponse(
    Long id,
    String name,
    BigDecimal price,
    Instant createdAt
) {}
```

### Test pattern
```java
@WebMvcTest(ItemController.class)  // for controller tests
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class) // for unit tests
@SpringBootTest                     // for integration tests only (slow — use sparingly)

// Use @MockBean in controller tests, @Mock in unit tests
// Always assert response status AND response body
// Test both happy path AND the most common error case minimum
```

## Files Agents Must NOT Modify
- `pom.xml` — no dependency changes without human review
- `src/main/resources/application.yml` — no config changes
- Any file with `// DO NOT MODIFY` in the first 5 lines

## Files Agents Should Read for Context
Before writing any new class, read:
- The interface the new class implements (if any)
- One existing example of the same type (e.g. read `OrderController.java` before writing `ItemController.java`)
- The relevant entity/model class

## Build Commands
```bash
mvn compile -q                          # compile only, quiet
mvn test -q                             # all tests
mvn test -Dtest=ItemControllerTest -q   # single test class
mvn verify -q                           # compile + test + package
```

